[{"category":"section","location":"#RandomFields","page":"Home","text":"Documentation for RandomFields.\n\n","title":"RandomFields"},{"category":"module","location":"#RandomFields.RandomFields","page":"Home","text":"Generate Gaussian Markov random fields with Matérn covariance functions on Oceananigans grids.\n\nAnisotropicMatern\nIsotropicMatern\nRandomFieldGenerator\ngenerate!\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RandomFields.RandomFields"},{"category":"type","location":"#RandomFields.AnisotropicMatern","page":"Home","text":"struct AnisotropicMatern{T, N} <: RandomFields.AbstractMaternParameters{T}\n\nParameters for an anisotropic Matérn covariance function with a per-dimension length-scale parameters.\n\nFields\n\nlength_scale::NTuple{N, T} where {T, N}: Tuple of length scale parameters, one per active dimension.\noutput_scale::Any: Scalar output scale parameter.\nsmoothness::Any: Scalar smoothness index - should be integer or half-integer.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RandomFields.AnisotropicMatern"},{"category":"type","location":"#RandomFields.IsotropicMatern","page":"Home","text":"struct IsotropicMatern{T} <: RandomFields.AbstractMaternParameters{T}\n\nParameters for an isotropic Matérn covariance function with a single length-scale parameter.\n\nFields\n\nlength_scale::Any: Scalar length scale parameter.\noutput_scale::Any: Scalar output scale parameter.\nsmoothness::Any: Scalar smoothness index - should be integer or half-integer.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RandomFields.IsotropicMatern"},{"category":"type","location":"#RandomFields.NonSeparableDirectionalOperator","page":"Home","text":"struct NonSeparableDirectionalOperator{M, I, A, V} <: RandomFields.AbstractDirectionalOperator{M, I}\n\nDirectional differential operator on a dimension M for grids with non-separable metrics.\n\nFields\n\ninner::Any: Derivative operation at dimension M flipped operand location\narea::Any: Face area operation at dimension M flipped operand location\nvolume::Any: Cell volume operation at operand location\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RandomFields.NonSeparableDirectionalOperator"},{"category":"type","location":"#RandomFields.RandomFieldGenerator","page":"Home","text":"struct RandomFieldGenerator{G, L, T, F, H, S}\n\nPrecomputed quantities and buffer storage for generating Gaussian random fields\n\nFields\n\ngrid::Any: Oceananigans grid fields will be generated on\nlocation::Any: Staggered grid location tuple fields will be generated on\nn_inverse_apply::Int64: Number of times inverse of modified Helmholtz linear operator is applied to generate field\nrequire_half_order::Bool: Whether the inverse half-order modified Helmholtz linear operator needs to be applied to generate field\nweights::Tuple{Vararg{T}} where T: Length-scale based weights for second derivative terms in modified Helmholtz operator\nfield_buffer_a::Any: Field buffer used to store intermediate quantities during computation\nfield_buffer_b::Any: Field buffer used to store intermediate quantities during computation\nwhite_noise_scale::Any: Field used to store precomputed per-cell scale factors for white noise generation\nmodified_helmholtz_operator::Any: Linear operator corresponding to modified Helmholtz equation for the parameters of interest\nsolver::Any: Solver for linear system in modified Helmholtz operator\nn_sqrt_quadrature_points::Int64: Number of quadrature points to use in integral approximation to square root of linear operator\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RandomFields.RandomFieldGenerator"},{"category":"method","location":"#RandomFields.RandomFieldGenerator-Tuple{Any, RandomFields.AbstractMaternParameters}","page":"Home","text":"RandomFieldGenerator(\n    field,\n    parameters;\n    reltol,\n    maxiter,\n    n_sqrt_quadrature_points\n)\n\n\nConstruct a random field generator for template field with covariance parameters parameters.\n\nThe linear systems are solved using a conjugate gradient solver with relative tolerance reltol and maximum number of iterations maxiter and the half-order (square-root) linear operator inverse is approximated using quadrature of an integral representation with n_sqrt_quadrature_points quadrature points if relevant.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RandomFields.RandomFieldGenerator"},{"category":"type","location":"#RandomFields.SeparableDirectionalOperator","page":"Home","text":"struct SeparableDirectionalOperator{M, I, D} <: RandomFields.AbstractDirectionalOperator{M, I}\n\nDirectional differential operator on a dimension M for grids with separable metrics.\n\nFields\n\ninner::Any: Derivative operation at dimension M flipped operand location\ndelta::Any: Grid spacing operation at operand location\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RandomFields.SeparableDirectionalOperator"},{"category":"function","location":"#RandomFields.bounding_pair","page":"Home","text":"bounding_pair(m, i, j, k)\n\nThe two indices, in (near, far) order, of the flipped-location evaluation points that bound a field's own location at indices (i, j, k) in dimension m.  Assumes loc is the output (field's own) location in dimension m.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RandomFields.bounding_pair"},{"category":"method","location":"#RandomFields.directional_operators-Tuple{Any, Any}","page":"Home","text":"directional_operators(grid, loc)\n\n\nConstruct directional differential operators for a field on a grid grid and with staggered grid locations tuple loc.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RandomFields.directional_operators"},{"category":"method","location":"#RandomFields.generate!-Tuple{Any, RandomFieldGenerator, Any}","page":"Home","text":"generate!(field, generator, noise)\n\n\nOverwrite field with an (approximate) draw from a mean-zero Gaussian random field with Matérn covariance, via the SPDE representation (1 - Σᵢλᵢ²∂ᵢ²)^(ν+d/2) f = τ w where λᵢ are per-dimension length scale parameters, ν a smoothness index, d the spatial dimension, f the field being solved for, τ an output scaling parameter and w a spatial white noise process. generator should be a RandomFieldGenerator built once via RandomFieldGenerator(field, parameters) and reusable across calls, with parameters an instance of IsotropicMatern or AnisotropicMatern and noise is an array of standard normal variates with size(noise) == size(field).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RandomFields.generate!"},{"category":"method","location":"#RandomFields.masked_evaluate-NTuple{7, Any}","page":"Home","text":"masked_evaluate(op, m, i, j, k, grid, operand)\n\n\nZero out a directional derivative  op evaluated at (i,j,k) on grid with operand if either of the two cells bounding that point (along dimension m) is solid.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RandomFields.masked_evaluate"},{"category":"function","location":"#RandomFields.second_derivative_term","page":"Home","text":"second_derivative_term(i, j, k, grid, op, far, near, flux_far, flux_near)\n\nCompute second derivative term for a field on grid grid with direction differential operator op at indices (i, j, k) given the computed flux terms flux_near and flux_far at near  and far offset index tuples far and near.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RandomFields.second_derivative_term"},{"category":"function","location":"#RandomFields.shift_index","page":"Home","text":"shift_index(m, i, j, k, offset)\n\nShift indices (i, j, k) by offset cells along dimension m.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RandomFields.shift_index"},{"category":"method","location":"#RandomFields.weighted_second_derivative_sum-Union{Tuple{D}, Tuple{L3}, Tuple{L2}, Tuple{L1}, Tuple{G}, Tuple{Any, Any, Any, G, Oceananigans.Fields.Field{L1, L2, L3}, NTuple{D, T} where T, NTuple{D, RandomFields.AbstractDirectionalOperator}}} where {G, L1, L2, L3, D}","page":"Home","text":"weighted_second_derivative_sum(\n    i,\n    j,\n    k,\n    grid,\n    operand,\n    weights,\n    operators\n)\n\n\nCompute the weighted second derivative sum for a field operand on grid grid at indices (i, j, k) with per-dimension derivative weights weights and directional derivative operators operators.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RandomFields.weighted_second_derivative_sum"},{"category":"method","location":"#RandomFields.zero!-Tuple{Oceananigans.Fields.Field}","page":"Home","text":"zero!(field)\n\n\nFill field with zeros in-place.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RandomFields.zero!"}]
